; Same fish-base vertex as flatten-opposite-ray-toward-b.bel (see its comment
; for the full derivation) — A′ even 4-ray stated form (both halves of the
; diagonal given, no derive), with the spine PINNED (`--ray & .c mountain`) so
; {toward} chooses only the side (approved rule 2026-07-19). `{toward .d}` picks
; the position class's other side under the rank-dipole stage, the MIRROR of that
; file: same face count, same table positions, opposite layer order (pinned
; by tests/test_flatten.ml's test_flatten_derive_opposite_ray_fish_base,
; which compares Fold_state.rank between the two toward points; `.bel`
; assertions can't express stacking, so `faces = 6` is what this file pins).

paper square

mark --diag = map .a onto .c
mark --ray = through .a .c

step left
mark --l1 = map --ab onto --diag
mark --l2 = map --da onto --diag
flatten (--l1) (--l2) (--ray & .a) (--ray & .c mountain) {toward .d}

; assert faces = 6
